WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:05.629
As traumatized fans of Game of Thrones know
all too well, Lady Catelyn Stark was shockingly

00:00:05.629 --> 00:00:10.050
and brutally slain in the penultimate episode
of season three. But with the show's final

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:15.140
season about to arrive, fans are once again
wondering: could she somehow still be alive?

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:19.800
On the surface, it sounds impossible. After
all, the infamous "Red Wedding" scene couldn't

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:24.450
have been more clear about the deaths of Catelyn,
her new daughter-in-law Talisa, and her son

00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:29.140
Robb Stark, the erstwhile King in the North.
After being betrayed by Lord Roose Bolton

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:33.560
and Lord Walder Frey who had been secretly
conspiring with the villainous House Lannister

00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:38.960
to destroy the Starks Robb, Talisa, and Catelyn
were all stabbed to death in horribly graphic

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:42.720
fashion. There's no doubt about it: she was
very definitely dead.

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:44.400
But is she going to stay dead?

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:49.740
"look who knows so much! Well, it just so
happens that your friend here is only mostly

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:54.000
dead. There's a big difference between mostly
dead and all dead."

00:00:54.590 --> 00:00:58.220
First, it's important to remember that people
come back from the dead in Game of Thrones

00:00:58.220 --> 00:01:02.910
all the time. Both Jon Snow and Beric Dondarrion
have done it thanks to the kiss of life from

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:07.960
the fire god known as the Lord of Light. And
then on the slightly less happy side of things,

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:12.700
the Night King has been resurrecting the dead
for eons, forming a zombie army that includes

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:15.080
not just giants, but a giant dragon.

00:01:15.290 --> 00:01:19.840
So it's theoretically possible that Catelyn
could be brought back. But more importantly,

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:24.630
it's actually already happened… in the books,
that is. Author George R. R. Martin, who wrote

00:01:24.630 --> 00:01:29.280
the fantasy novels that form the basis for
Game of Thrones, resurrected Catelyn not long

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:33.920
after the Red Wedding, with Beric Dondarrion
surrendering his own immortality in order

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:37.960
to return Catelyn to the land of the living
as the vengeful Lady Stoneheart.

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:42.560
For her part, actress Michelle Fairley told
Entertainment Weekly that Catelyn would not

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:45.260
be returning regardless of what happened in
the books.

00:01:45.260 --> 00:01:50.080
"Yeah, the character's dead. She's dead. You
respect the writers' decision. I knew the

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:54.229
arc, and that was it. They can't stick to
the books 100 percent. It's impossible…

00:01:54.229 --> 00:01:58.410
they only have 10 hours per season. They have
got to keep it dramatic and exciting, and

00:01:58.410 --> 00:02:02.810
extraneous stuff along the way gets lost in
order to maintain the quality of brilliant

00:02:02.810 --> 00:02:03.300
show."

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:08.000
Still, people associated with Game of Thrones
have been known to lie in the past in order

00:02:08.009 --> 00:02:13.629
to prevent spoilers. Most famously, for example,
the folks at HBO swore up and down for a year

00:02:13.629 --> 00:02:18.540
that Jon Snow was actually, really dead for
good after being betrayed at the end of season

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:22.360
5. Naturally, of course, he was back on his
feet in season 6.

00:02:22.360 --> 00:02:27.690
Plus, even some of the show's stars have publicly
hinted that more major characters would be

00:02:27.690 --> 00:02:33.430
also brought back from the grave on the side
of the Night King. In 2017, Nikolaj Coster-Waldau,

00:02:33.430 --> 00:02:35.440
who plays Jaime Lannister, told Esquire

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:39.780
"The fear is that I would be turned into one
of those undead. That would suck. You know

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:43.760
some of the main characters are going to get
turned. There are going to be some blue-eyed

00:02:43.779 --> 00:02:47.340
main characters running around. And, god,
I hope it's not me."

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:51.549
Some fans, though, think that Catelyn has
already re-appeared as Lady Stoneheart in

00:02:51.549 --> 00:02:56.120
season 7, passing through the background of
a scene at Winterfell at the same moment her

00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:57.620
daughter, Arya, mentioned her.

00:02:57.720 --> 00:03:01.580
"You swore to serve both my mother's daughters,
didn't you?"

00:03:02.380 --> 00:03:06.959
And others believe the first season 8 teaser,
which shows the Stark children gathered in

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:09.720
the family crypt, hints at Catelyn's return.

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:16.100
"all the horror that has come to my family,
it's all because I couldn't love a motherless

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:16.600
child."

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:22.580
But It still seems pretty unlikely that Catelyn
will ever return. Don't worry, though. Game

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:27.529
of Thrones has plenty of big fish to fry,
dangling plot threads to tie up, and mysteries

00:03:27.529 --> 00:03:32.239
to solve in its final six episodes — so
even if Cat never makes a surprise return,

00:03:32.239 --> 00:03:37.150
viewers will have lots of juicy storylines
to sink their teeth into when season 8 premieres

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:39.460
on HBO on Sunday, April 14.

